00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.930
Every call sign is gonna be
something unique and weird

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.240
about you or something that you did,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.670
which is borderline
embarrassing/humiliating.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:01.670
If you were to go into a place and say,

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.520
I want my call sign to be Maverick,

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.832
you would probably be hazed
to the point of death.

00:08:05.832 --> 00:08:10.832
(door squeaking)
(upbeat pop music)

00:08:13.119 --> 00:08:16.430
(bell chiming)

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:17.730
Don't do this.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.563
Don't do this.

00:08:18.563 --> 00:08:20.690
- But they had a connection.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:24.560
- So, eh, I have no
doubt in Maverick's mind

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.490
that he has a special
connection with this lady

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.900
and that this was an
invitation with her eyes,

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.180
for him to come join
her in the ladies' room.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.110
Let me put it this way.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.220
He's probably breaking
at least three laws here.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.720
Let's assume for a second

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.150
that this poor woman

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:43.490
had no intention of inviting
Maverick into the ladies' room.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:44.880
- [Devin] I think that's
probably safe to say, yeah.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.700
- Yeah, so he's basically committing

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.560
a couple different crimes.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.000
One, conduct unbecoming
an officer or gentleman.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.490
This is so basic.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.900
That is literally the text of the statute,

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:58.570
conduct unbecoming, an
officer or a gentleman.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.790
All it requires to show is

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.600
that he's doing something
indecent, immoral,

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.803
something wrong.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.020
It's also probably prejudicial
to good order and discipline,

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.760
or has a tendency to
discredit the Armed Forces,

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.830
which is a violation of Article 134

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.640
of the Uniformed Code of Military Justice.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.460
- Yeah, well, it sounds bad
when you put it that way.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.230
- I mean, he's in uniform, on base.

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:23.697
This kind of behavior is
really dangerous for him.

00:09:23.697 --> 00:09:26.060
- She has a PhD in astrophysics

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.790
and she's also a civilian contractor.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.780
So you do not salute her,

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:30.613
but you better listen to her

00:09:30.613 --> 00:09:33.430
because the Pentagon listens
to her about your proficiency.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:34.467
It's all yours, Charlie.

00:09:34.467 --> 00:09:35.467
- Thank you.

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.420
Hello?

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.900
- Okay, so is it at all realistic

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.110
that there would be a civilian who

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.540
is some sort of contractor

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.820
that would be providing some instruction

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.940
to the pilots at Top Gun?

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.330
- I don't think it's unusual

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:55.330
or I don't think it's so
unusual that it's unrealistic.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.080
We have civilian contractors
everywhere in the military

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.410
doing a wide variety of things

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:04.080
and especially people who
have specific training

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.160
and experience like having
a PhD in astrophysics.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.200
I'm sure that they could
be useful to some extent,

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.330
probably not talking about tactics,

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:15.510
but talking about the
aerodynamics of the aircraft,

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.050
things like that.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.490
- I'm not sure that astrophysics

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.170
would help with aerodynamics.

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:23.120
I think-
- Was it astrophysics?

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.510
- PhD in astrophysics?

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.550
- They said, yeah, they said astrophysics.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.750
So unless they're charting with the stars,

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:32.940
I'm not sure her PhD is
gonna help that much.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.140
I guess we're assuming that she has

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.500
a bunch of other experience
in the private sector

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.750
that led her to this expertise.

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:40.490
- Well, you know, it
is possible, I suppose,

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.108
that "Top Gun 2" is
actually gonna be in space.

00:10:43.108 --> 00:10:44.060
- Yes!

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.200
Yes.
(Spencer laughing)

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.469
In space.

00:10:46.469 --> 00:10:47.880
(electronic whirring)

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.203
- Welcome to the

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.830
danger zone.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.070
- That's classified.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:54.903
- It's what?

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:56.793
- It's classified.

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.420
I could tell you, but
then I'd have to kill you.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.640
- Lieutenant, I have top secret clearance.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.480
The Pentagon sees to it
that I know more than you.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.380
- Yeah, okay.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:10.570
So, (laughs) I've never
been in the military,

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:14.570
but I do have a lot of friends
who have TS/SCI clearance

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:18.480
and she might have that kind of clearance,

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.680
but none of them necessarily
have TS/SCI, right.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:24.880
Like, I don't think all of those pilots

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.350
are necessarily gonna have the clearance

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:27.290
to be able to hear what,

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.800
he just said, he can't tell people

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.770
without that particular clearance.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:31.603
- I mean, yeah.

00:11:31.603 --> 00:11:35.080
I would assume every single
officer has secret clearance

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.350
at least, okay.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:39.440
But getting TS/SCI is actually
somewhat more unusual,

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.850
costs a lot of money

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.420
and actually has quite a bit
of value on the private sector

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.650
once you leave the military.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:45.750
- Yes, I have heard that.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.210
- I will say this, for all
of you who are watching,

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:51.350
if you have a little bit
of classified information

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.000
that you're not allowed to tell anyone,

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.550
and a civilian just
tells you, oh, it's okay,

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:56.956
I have security clearance, too.

00:11:56.956 --> 00:11:57.910
(Devin laughing)

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.380
Do not,

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:03.390
do not give them that
classified information.

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:04.820
It's gonna be a bad day for you

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:06.490
if that person does not in fact

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:07.520
have that security clearance.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.140
- [Goose] No, no, ma'am
this is not a good idea.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.450
- [Maverick] Sorry, Goose.

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:13.054
But it's time to buzz the tower.

00:12:13.054 --> 00:12:14.992
(jet engine whirring)

00:12:14.992 --> 00:12:18.217
(upbeat music)

00:12:18.217 --> 00:12:20.053
- Goddamn, this son of a bitch.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.890
- All right, that seems super bad.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.450
- Yeah, as Maverick's defense attorney,

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.060
I've gotta say, he
needs to, at this point,

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.990
not say anything to anyone

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.030
about what just happened,

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:33.890
lock himself into a room
and hope for the best.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:37.000
- So yeah, what did he just do there?

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.160
- A number of crimes.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.100
I mean, honestly, this
is one of those cases

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:43.660
where he could get racked up
on maybe five different counts.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.200
He certainly, willfully disobeyed

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.829
the order of a superior
commissioned officer.

00:12:47.829 --> 00:12:48.662
(bell chimes)

00:12:48.662 --> 00:12:49.780
There's another article at the UCMJ

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:52.110
about drunken or reckless operation

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.610
of an aircraft.
(bell chimes)

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:54.620
There's another one,

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.350
reckless endangerment.
(bell chimes)

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.967
There's another, conduct
unbecoming an officer

00:12:57.967 --> 00:12:59.410
and a gentleman.
(bell chimes)

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.343
Improperly hazarding an aircraft.

00:13:01.343 --> 00:13:02.176
(bell chimes)

00:13:02.176 --> 00:13:03.880
Some of those could
carry the death penalty.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.610
The reality is some of those
would be harder to prove,

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:07.780
some would be easier.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.870
The one that he absolutely just did

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.420
is disobeying that order.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.510
And that's a bad, bad thing for him.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.060
- Yeah, it seems like in the military,

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.920
you kind of have to follow orders.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:20.110
- We follow orders or people die.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.160
- You know, it's strongly suggested.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.810
And unfortunately, in the real world,

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.320
not only would he get grounded,

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.780
he would probably lose his wings entirely

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.560
and spend the rest of
his time on his contract,

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:32.930
like filling sandbags

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:36.500
or doing something very
menial in an office.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.333
- Sounds about right.

00:13:37.333 --> 00:13:38.590
- That's because every
time you go open the air,

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:40.010
you're unsafe.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:41.910
I don't like you because you're dangerous.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:42.743
- That's right.

00:13:43.838 --> 00:13:45.123
Iceman.

00:13:46.374 --> 00:13:47.453
I am dangerous.

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:51.220
(teeth chatter)

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.250
- That's what we call an admission.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.930
And unfortunately for him,
it is absolutely true.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.100
And goes back to some
of the reckless things

00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.770
that he's been doing this entire time.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:02.170
Again, as Maverick's defense attorney,

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:04.970
I strongly advise him to remain silent

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:06.380
when it comes to this kind of stuff.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:10.320
- Okay, so that reminds
me of a certain fan theory

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.160
about "Top Gun",

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.670
which is that "Top Gun"
is really a love story

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.140
between two characters,

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.800
not Tom Cruise and Kelly McGillis,

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.920
but rather, Tom Cruise's character

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.523
and Val Kilmer's character, Iceman.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:32.070
If, let's say Maverick and
Iceman were not married,

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.290
but then decided to

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.870
have a relationship with each other,

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:41.590
would that violate any rules of the UCMJ?

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.860
- So what it would probably violate

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.840
would be a regulation that says

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.500
people who are on the same command

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.570
cannot have intimate relationships.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.530
Now, if they, because they're
both at the Top Gun school,

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.530
you're not allowed to have
an intimate relationship

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:58.110
just because of the way that
that could impact the school,

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:00.050
the command, et cetera.

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:02.160
However, once they're outside of Top Gun,

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.950
as long as they're not in the same unit,

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:06.260
they can have the most
wonderful relationship

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.630
that they could possibly want.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:09.886
And I wish them the best.
(Devin laughing)

00:15:09.886 --> 00:15:13.821
♪ Take my breath away ♪

00:15:13.821 --> 00:15:15.370
- You can be my wing man, anytime.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.280
- You know, funny story,

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.420
I actually was a military prosecutor

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:21.870
signed to what is now Marine
Corps Air Station Miramar.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:25.260
And I watched at least
one pilot get prosecuted.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.510
One pilot got entirely
dismissed from the Marine Corps.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:32.120
He was a test pilot for an
F-35 and it was for adultery.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.820
He got kicked out for adultery.

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:37.307
- So I mean, that's not a crime (laughs),

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.800
for civilians, that's a
crime for service members?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.920
- It absolutely is.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:47.230
And it is actually a
frighteningly common crime

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.470
for service members.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:52.500
Now it's not enough that you had an affair

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.400
when you're married

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:56.970
or you had an affair with
someone who is married.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.483
There has to be something
additional to it.

00:15:58.483 --> 00:15:59.900
- Huh.
- It has to be either

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.810
prejudicial to good order and discipline,

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.660
or have a tendency to
discredit the Armed Forces.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:06.612
But in adultery cases,

00:16:06.612 --> 00:16:08.770
(sighs) they're not that hard to show and-

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:11.640
- Yeah, I mean, so why would adultery

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.223
be something that the
military cares about?

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.380
- Well, for one, there are
a lot of moralistic prigs

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.520
who are in the military,

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.070
but the other part of it is,

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.960
you really can't have people,

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.660
especially in the same chain of command

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.060
or on the same base,

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:27.200
who are themselves
married and having affairs

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.910
with other people on the base.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:30.410
- Ah.
- So for example,

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.910
let's say that you're a
captain like Maverick,

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:35.210
you're single, but you
decide to have an affair

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.370
with someone who's married on the base

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.110
and that person is a civilian,

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:41.950
but married to another
officer, for example.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.760
That can cause real tensions

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:46.530
inside of the base, inside of the command.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:49.180
And that is prejudicial to
good order and discipline

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.530
because you're introducing
so much possibility

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:55.240
for anger, recrimination.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.240
It's just something you
want to avoid entirely.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.830
- Sir.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.733
I had Commander Heatherly in my sites.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:03.970
He saw me move in for the kill.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:07.440
He then proceeded below the hard deck.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:10.940
We weren't below 10,000 for
more than a few seconds.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.210
I had the shot.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.030
There was no danger so I took it.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.350
- So here's the problem with this,

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.800
what he did by going
underneath the hard deck

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.460
was a violation of the regulations.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:22.680
But also let's talk about what
the hard deck really meant

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.500
in this context.
- Yeah, what does that mean?

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:27.030
- The hard deck simulates the ground.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.560
So when he says that he
went beneath the hard deck,

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.070
only for a few seconds,

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:32.700
that's like saying in your aircraft,

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.610
you went beneath the ground
for a couple seconds.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.440
(Devin laughing)

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.160
That hard deck is there
for everyone's safety,

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:41.300
so that you have lots of buffer room

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.380
in a training environment.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.830
And for him to just be underneath
it for a couple seconds,

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.080
well, you know, I'm sure
the aircraft will be fine

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.750
underneath the desert of California

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.583
for a couple seconds.

00:17:50.583 --> 00:17:52.520
- It's an aircraft and a submarine.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.630
- Yep.
- That's how good we are.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.880
- We're getting there guys.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:59.470
- The communication ship SS
Layton has become disabled

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.040
and has wandered in the foreign territory.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.310
Rescue operation is to
begin within the hour.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.810
Your mission is to give
air support to that rescue.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:10.600
- So this is kind of a complicated setup.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.780
We're obviously, tensions are high

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.640
and there's the possibility of war

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.290
or some sort of hostile act here

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.770
where we actually are gonna see combat.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:23.720
Now we have to assume that
what that means in the film

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:25.170
is that this ship has drifted

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.700
into what are called territorial waters.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.640
Now, territorial waters for
any country on the ocean,

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.960
they extend about 12 miles out.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:35.100
But because the law of the sea,

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.210
there's an exception to that,

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.930
which is called innocent passage.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.880
So what innocent passage means is

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.900
if another ship goes through

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.300
and all they're doing is going to port

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.770
or going through those territorial waters

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:48.700
with innocent motives,

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:49.930
then you can't just attack them.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.870
It's not an invasion of the
country or anything like that.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.380
Now what they can do, of course,

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.980
is they can police their
territorial waters.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:01.390
So someone comes in for,
on innocent passage,

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:02.980
you can board them, you can search them.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.910
You can do a variety
of things to make sure

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.850
that it is in fact innocent passage.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:07.950
So the problem is

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.000
that while there's innocent
passage in the sea,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.290
there is no such thing as
innocent passage in the air.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.560
The second that a US combat
aircraft goes into the airspace

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:19.210
above another country's
territorial waters,

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:22.200
that could be very clearly
seen as an act of war.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.190
- Oh, well, that complicates
things a lot, I think.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:26.550
- Yeah, yeah.

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.740
- So what you're saying is
that the American planes

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:30.710
are entering into a

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.233
zone of danger,

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:37.875
a sort of danger zone.

00:19:37.875 --> 00:19:41.723
- (laughing) They are in fact
going into the danger zone.

00:19:42.895 --> 00:19:43.728
♪ Danger zone ♪

00:19:43.728 --> 00:19:45.479
♪ Danger zone ♪
(Spencer laughing)

00:19:45.479 --> 00:19:49.010
(jet engine whirring)

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:49.983
- Goddamn it.

00:19:49.983 --> 00:19:53.280
- All right, so we've already talked about

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:56.550
how much of a blatant
violation buzzing the tower is

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.730
back in Miramar.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:02.930
Assuming that they
weren't run out on rail,

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.310
what would happen if they
buzzed a tower again,

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:07.620
after being reprimanded the first time?

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:08.890
- Nothing good.
(Devin laughing)

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:11.020
In fact, very, very bad things.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.370
I think it's safe to
say that at this point,

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.160
Maverick is not just gonna
be stripped of his wings,

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:19.520
but he's probably gonna get
dismissed from the service.

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.103
- And also on top of it,

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:25.010
we're at war now.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:29.260
This unidentified country has
shot down an American plane.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:31.130
I think by all reasonable accounts,

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:33.940
that means that we are
at war with this country.

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:37.240
Seems like a really super
bad time to be showboating.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.073
- Absolutely.

00:20:38.073 --> 00:20:39.290
And the reality is, I mean,

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.280
we do find out slightly later in this film

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.870
that this other country
is gonna decide that,

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:46.080
hey, it's no big deal,

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:48.270
but we don't know that right now.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:52.090
Everyone on this aircraft
carrier has to assume

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:55.400
that we are at war right
now with this country.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.900
And yet, we're doing a fly by.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:58.953
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:20:58.953 --> 00:21:01.710
That, so, yeah, that seems bad.

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:03.132
- Suboptimal.

00:21:03.132 --> 00:21:03.965
(crowd cheering)

00:21:03.965 --> 00:21:06.282
(men yelling)

00:21:06.282 --> 00:21:07.450
(crowd cheering)

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:11.080
Somewhere, there is a chief
petty officer in the Navy

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.593
screaming and sobbing into a pillow.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:16.870
The fact that we are in war right now,

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.280
or at least we have to
assume that we're in war

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:22.530
and the entire deck crew
is abandoning their posts,

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.750
running out to celebrate these guys,

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:25.800
when for all we know,

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.090
there's a bunch of other MiGs

